## 2. 9-item rubric score (canonical phrasing: `6/6 verifier + 1 HITL + 1 flip`)

| Group | Item | Verdict | Notes |
|-------|------|---------|-------|
| A — verifier | 1 — methodology doc | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.1 |
| A — verifier | 2 — intent doc + version bump | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.2 |
| A — verifier | 4 — regression suite + behavior-vs-tautology sub-check | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.3 |
| A — verifier | 6 — paired-wiki integrity + atomicity sub-check | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.4 |
| A — verifier | 8 — end-to-end run + run-success sub-check | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.5 |
| A — verifier | 9 — node-type discipline | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §3.6 |
| B — promotion | 3 — YAML status | `<pending flip \| live>` | see §5 |
| B — promotion | 5 — compliance-verifier PASS | `<PASS \| FAIL>` | see §5 |
| B — promotion | 7 — operator HITL (4-stage per op-guard-32) | `<awaiting operator \| CONFIRM / ACHIEVES / PASS / PROMOTE>` | see §5 |

**Audit score:** `<N>/6 verifier + <HITL-dispositioned-yes/no> + <flipped-yes/no>` (per Part 3 canonical phrasing). Do NOT use "9/9" or "8/8" — those framings conflate the 3 distinct concerns.

